    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** anchoring the lineup, both posting elite efficiency scores above 79. **Gunnar Henderson** (81.36) is our strongest play; he draws a favorable matchup against Tong, benefiting from a massive 14% boost due to dynamic platoon advantage and high SP-skill projections. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (79.25) remains a priority start despite facing Lodolo, as the SP-skill adjustment (+17%) and his placement in the cleanup spot keep his production floor high. **Jackson Merrill** also presents significant upside today (75.27); he is the primary beneficiary of a stadium park factor (+14%) and a soft matchup against Sugano, making him a high-leverage target to chase counting stats in our pursuit of 5x5 category gains.\n\nManaging our roster depth remains challenging, specifically regarding the corner infield spots where **Miguel Vargas** (40.41) and **Coby Mayo** (50.91) are teetering near the bench threshold. **Miguel Vargas** was nearly relegated to the bench today, saved only by his favorable lineup placement in the #3 spot; his score is significantly suppressed by the 2.89 xERA of Williams, who represents the toughest pitching matchup on our card. While the optimizer suggests caution, the scarcity of options\u2014exacerbated by the continued injury status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**\u2014forces us to lean on these moderate-upside bats. **Wade Meckler** (40.39) is the closest to a benching; his score is hampered by a difficult lefty-on-lefty matchup and a suboptimal #9 spot in the order, though he remains active to protect our game caps until replacements like **Heliot Ramos** or **Nasim Nunez** become more viable utility alternatives. We are monitoring these low-efficiency spots closely, as players like **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Curtis Mead** remain on the periphery, waiting for a breakout or a defensive injury that would necessitate a roster shuffle.",
